+# SANDOP-CAPACITY semantics v2.0.0 — publication candidate, NOT APPROVED
+
+This annex belongs to `sandop-capacity.openapi.candidate.yaml` only. Proposed metadata `info.version: 2.0.0`, wire `contractVersion: v1`. The major version is a **release proposal** because state eligibility, new error cases and source-reference rejection can narrow behavior; metadata alone does not negotiate routes or migrate consumers. No canonical publication, owner consent or runtime uptake follows from this artifact. The only recorded human-approved shared boundaries are the test-only DEMAND fixture, local JWT actor/no Workflow, atomic Pending-only outbox/no Event Bus publisher, and fixture-only Capacity constraints/results. D190-04/05 and C192-02…07 in the policy packs were marked unapproved when inspected; the present user request authorizes candidate preparation but does not itself supply an exact prior approval record. The recommendations below therefore remain **candidate decisions** until owner source is bound.
+
+## Common transport, error, receipt and precedence proposal
+
+All twelve operations require bearer authentication and a single valid UUID `X-Correlation-Id`. The three S&OP and three Capacity POSTs require a nonempty parsed `Idempotency-Key`. Key identity is **exact parsed string**: no trim, case folding, max-200 rule or silent Unicode normalization. `CreateSandopPlanRequest.name` likewise retains its frozen minimum length 1 with no new trim/maximum; a 201-character key or name is not rejected solely for length. Standard host request-size limits are separate transport limits. The body remains the frozen schema with `additionalProperties:false` where declared. No new endpoint or body field is introduced.
+
+Precedence candidate: authentication parser (401) → trusted tenant/LE and operation grant (403) → required headers/body schema (400) → scoped target existence (404) → durable receipt identity/fingerprint → current state/duplicate/fixture validation (declared 409/422) → atomic commit. Cross-scope target is 404 and cannot expose a receipt. A valid same-key receipt replays before a later state change or fixture reread; changed valid payload is 409 `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED` before current business conflicts. Invalid payload never retrieves an old success. Reads have no receipt. All failures leave no new write, except unresolved unknown commit, whose result is unknown until durable receipt resolution.
+
+Receipt tuple: `(TenantId, LegalEntityId, operationId, targetId-or-create-sentinel, exact parsed key)`. Actor and correlation are excluded. SHA-256 fingerprint is over canonical decoded JSON: object member order/escape spelling normalized; array order and exact Unicode string/decimal lexemes retained; omitted and null distinct (null rejected if schema forbids); operation/target are in tuple. No TTL/key reuse in the bounded slice. A different authorized actor can replay the original result without rewriting original audit actor. No `idempotentReplay` field or new response body shape is added.
+
+Identical valid same-key request returns the stored **original status/body** (201 for create/capture/sign-off/scenario, 202 for evaluate) without dependency reread or second aggregate/receipt/audit/outbox/job. Response `X-Correlation-Id` is the **current request's** valid UUID; original persisted audit/event correlation stays original. An error generated now carries current UUID in `Error.error.correlationId` and header. A retry with a different correlation but identical payload therefore gets original business body and current header. Auth failure happens before receipt. Missing/malformed/duplicate correlation proposes 400 `INVALID_CORRELATION_ID`, no write, and one generated rejection-only UUID in response header/body because no unique valid request UUID can be echoed; this is a proposed explicit exception to the old echo description. Parser-level malformed wire bytes may be rejected before application body; they must not be called an application-envelope PASS.
+
+Response shape for all application errors: frozen `#/components/schemas/Error` (`{error:{code,message,correlationId,details?},contractVersion:'v1'}`); success bodies and their required/null rules remain unchanged. New 401 includes `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`; 403 is `FORBIDDEN`. Generic malformed body/header is 400 `INVALID_REQUEST`. Dependency/storage failure is 503 `DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE`. For mutation uncertain commit, query durable receipt first: found → original result; unresolved → 503 `COMMIT_RESULT_UNRESOLVED` and same-key recovery after restart; never assert zero writes from the 503 alone. Known precommit failure rolls aggregate/receipt/audit/Pending outbox back. GET storage failure can use 503 `DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE`, never the mutation-only unknown-commit code. Exact code/message text in candidate YAML examples is proposed, not published.
+
+## Twelve-operation status/error matrix
+
+For every row, 400/401/403 follow the common rule above; 503 is `DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE` for known dependency/storage failure, plus `COMMIT_RESULT_UNRESOLVED` on POST only. Valid response/error correlation and headers follow the common rule. Frozen response codes are listed before proposed additions; no prior frozen code is removed.
+
+| operationId / path | Frozen success and business failure | Candidate added/special failure | Replay and acceptance example |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `createSandopPlan` POST `/sandop-plans` | 201 Draft/currentSnapshotId null; 409 `SANDOP_PLAN_ALREADY_EXISTS`; 422 `INVALID_DEMAND_REFERENCE` | 409 `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED`; common 400/401/403/503 | Exact fixture Published ID/version 201; unknown/unpublished 422, zero writes. Same key/body original 201, changed name 409 key-reused. |
+| `getSandopPlan` GET `/sandop-plans/{sandopPlanId}` | 200; 404 `UNKNOWN_SANDOP_PLAN` | common 400/401/403/503 | Scoped read returns Draft then InReview after capture; foreign tenant/LE 404. No replay. |
+| `captureSandopSnapshot` POST `/sandop-plans/{sandopPlanId}/snapshots` | 201; 404 `UNKNOWN_SANDOP_PLAN`; 409 `SANDOP_PLAN_STATE_CONFLICT`; 422 `INVALID_DEMAND_REFERENCE` | 409 `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED`; common 400/401/403/503 | Draft or InReview → immutable snapshot, plan InReview; Approved/Rejected/Archived → declared 409. Exact fixture checksum mismatch → 422 `INVALID_DEMAND_REFERENCE`, zero writes. Same key/body returns original snapshot. |
+| `listSandopSnapshots` GET same `/snapshots` | 200; 404 `UNKNOWN_SANDOP_PLAN` | common 400/401/403/503 | Lists old and new snapshots with provenance unchanged; foreign plan 404. No replay. |
+| `recordSandopSignOff` POST `/sandop-plans/{sandopPlanId}/sign-offs` | 201; 404 `UNKNOWN_SANDOP_PLAN`; 409 `SIGN_OFF_ALREADY_RECORDED`; 422 `INVALID_SNAPSHOT_REFERENCE` | 409 `SANDOP_SIGN_OFF_STATE_CONFLICT` for non-InReview; 409 `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED`; common 400/401/403/503 | InReview, any same-plan snapshot and frozen role/decision → 201, immutable sign-off; duplicate same snapshot/role different key → one 201, one 409. Same-key retry original 201. Draft/Approved/Rejected/Archived 409 state conflict; wrong-plan snapshot 422. |
+| `listSandopSignOffs` GET same `/sign-offs` | 200; 404 `UNKNOWN_SANDOP_PLAN` | common 400/401/403/503 | Lists decisions across same-plan snapshots without overwriting. No replay. |
+| `createCapacityPlan` POST `/capacity-plans` | 201 Draft; 409 `CAPACITY_PLAN_ALREADY_EXISTS`; 422 `INVALID_DEMAND_REFERENCE` | 409 `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED`; common 400/401/403/503 | Exact scoped Published ID/version/checksum fixture 201; checksum mismatch 422, zero writes; same key/body original 201. |
+| `getCapacityPlan` GET `/capacity-plans/{capacityPlanId}` | 200; 404 `UNKNOWN_CAPACITY_PLAN` | common 400/401/403/503 | Scoped Draft provenance read; foreign scope 404. No replay. |
+| `createCapacityScenario` POST `/capacity-plans/{capacityPlanId}/scenarios` | 201 Draft; 404 `UNKNOWN_CAPACITY_PLAN`; 409 `CAPACITY_PLAN_STATE_CONFLICT` | 422 `INVALID_CONSTRAINT_REFERENCE` for unknown/stale/cross-scope/mismatched fixture tuple; 409 `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED`; common 400/401/403/503 | Exact `(tenant,LE,source,id,version,resource,period,UoM)` fixture 201; altered tuple or UoM 422 and zero writes; same key/body original 201. |
+| `getCapacityScenario` GET `/capacity-plans/{capacityPlanId}/scenarios/{scenarioId}` | 200; 404 `UNKNOWN_CAPACITY_SCENARIO` | common 400/401/403/503 | Same plan/scoped scenario only; foreign scope 404. No replay. |
+| `evaluateCapacityScenario` POST `/capacity-plans/{capacityPlanId}/scenarios/{scenarioId}/evaluations` | 202 Accepted; 404 `UNKNOWN_CAPACITY_SCENARIO`; 409 `EVALUATION_ALREADY_ACTIVE` | 409 `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED`; common 400/401/403/503 | Different key while Accepted/Running → declared 409; same key/body original 202, no second job. Terminal fixture-only Completed/Failed is not a general optimizer claim. |
+| `getCapacityEvaluation` GET `/capacity-plans/{capacityPlanId}/evaluations/{evaluationId}` | 200; 404 `UNKNOWN_CAPACITY_EVALUATION` | common 400/401/403/503 | Read Accepted/Running/Completed/Failed without mutation; foreign scope 404. No replay. |
+
+## Lifecycle/fixture boundary that candidate wire errors depend on
+
+0190: Create Draft/null; capture from Draft or InReview appends immutable snapshot and sets InReview; sign-off only InReview against any same-plan snapshot, one decision per snapshot/role, no automatic plan Approved/Rejected even after all five roles approve. The new sign-off state-conflict code needs owner and contract release. 0192: Capacity plan/scenario remain Draft in this bounded slice; evaluation alone may progress Accepted→Running→Completed/Failed under a **separately approved** module-owned executor. The C192 proposal of startup+10-second scan, 30-second fenced lease and three attempts remains unapproved in inspected records. Terminal values come only from the exact fixture oracle `CAPACITY-EVAL-FIXTURE-192-01@1`; no live optimizer, supply-constraint source or Event Bus publisher. A Pending outbox event is written at terminal commit, no publisher delivery claim. With no approved executor, terminal E4 acceptance remains HELD.
+
+The four approved scope limits are respected: exact tenant/LE test fixture for DEMAND with no producer endpoint; local trusted JWT actor/no Workflow; atomic Pending outbox/no publisher; Capacity fixture references/literal results only. A fixture PASS is not live DEMAND version/checksum or constraint producer validation. New 400/409/422/503 cases and the exact executor/lifecycle/replay policies are candidate amendments, not an assertion that those later proposals had already been approved.
+
+## Acceptance controls for independent VER
+
+1. Verify baseline and candidate hashes, exact patch application and only this YAML/annex candidate scope; compare operationId/path/security/body schemas/event schemas to baseline. No DEMAND YAML edit.
+2. Validate OpenAPI 3.1 schema, local refs and every positive/negative response example. For each of twelve rows exercise schema/model status/code/body/header/correlation positive and negative fixtures; a duplicate key and checksum mismatch fixture must detect incorrect behavior, not merely restate expected values.
+3. Compare 12 operation count, six S&OP/six Capacity, no new endpoint, no removed success/business status, no shared schema change except explicit new response components and `info.version`/annex pointer.
+4. Distinguish these schema/model checks from real HTTP/JWT/Mongo, producer uptake, consumer consent, guard, publication, pack promotion or rollout.
